<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pennal Letter</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1406</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Pennal Letter was written by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/owain-glyndwr">Owain Glyndŵr</a> at Pennal on 31 March 1406 to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-vi-of-france">Charles VI of France</a>. In it Glyndŵr offered to transfer the allegiance of the Welsh Church from the pope in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> to the pope in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/avignon">Avignon</a> in return for French support, and set out plans for an independent Welsh Church and two universities. It survives in the French national archives.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pennal-letter.jpg" alt="Pennal Letter" width="320" height="502" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Tipcake · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ffacsimili_Llythyr_Pennal,_Senedd-dy_Owain_Glynd%C5%B5r,_Machynlleth.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
